# Kairo Formatter — Style Rules (draft)


 > Line width: 100 columns.


### 1. Argument/parameter list wrapping

If a parenthesized list `(item1, item2, ...)` would exceed the line width on one line, break it — one item per line, aligned to the column just after the opening paren:
```rs
fn example(
    item1,
    item2,
    item3,
    ...
    itemLast 
   )
```



### 2. Multiline assignment aligning

For multiline assignmenst or declarations with : and = 
format will be converted to 

```rs
item1      = 67
item2      = 34
itemscount = 56
tree       = "binary"

var item1      : u32
var itemscount : u8
var item2      : u32
var tree       : string
```



### 3. Blank line preservation

Preserve up to 4 consecutive blank lines from source; collapse anything beyond that down to 4. Configurable via `--blankline=preserve` (flag name/behavior subject to change).



### 4. Comment relocation

Because reformatting changes line counts, a trailing comment is re-anchored to the line where its associated node starts, not where it originally sat:

```rs
fn example(item1, item2, item3, ...itemLast)   // hello mate 
```
becomes, once wrapped:

```rs
fn example(  
    item1,   // hello mate
    item2,
    item3,
    ...
    itemLast
)
```